{
  "reasoning": "A and B are brothers; C and D are sisters. Their children X and Y are double first cousins (they share both paternal and maternal grandparents). Children of first cousins are second cousins; children of double first cousins inherit twice the shared ancestry, making them double second cousins. Therefore P and Q are double second cousins.",
  "answer": "D"
}
